Read the description of the files at http://kbroman.org/qtl2/assets/vignettes/input_files.html

The yaml file is the "control file". Open it with a text editor, such as atom https://atom.io
You should also be able to open it in RStudio.

You need at least a physical map for your markers; you could use that to estimate the genetic map. R/qtl2 doesn't include facilities for de novo map construction.

karl

